p.src:
The state vectors are not themselves observables. To define an observable, associate numerical records with the two possible outcomes. Following the lecture, record $+1$ for $x$-polarization and $-1$ for $y$-polarization. The corresponding operator obeys $\hat P_{xy}\ket x=+\ket x,
  \qquad
  \hat P_{xy}\ket y=-\ket y.$ In the $(\ket x,\ket y)$ basis, $\hat P_{xy}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    1&0\\
    0&-1
  \end{pmatrix}
  =\ket x\bra x-\ket y\bra y.$

